      "q": "1. Fill in the Blanks:\n(a) Production of a new individual from the vegetative parts of the parent is called\n__________\n.",
      "a": "Vegetative propagation\n(b) A flower may have either male or female reproductive parts. Such a flower is called\n________\n.\nAns:\nUnisexual flowers\n(c) The transfer of pollen grains from the anther to the stigma of the same or of another flower of the same kind is known as________.\nAns:\nPollination\n(d) The fusion of male and female gametes is termed as_________.\nAns\n: Fertilisation\n(e) Seed dispersal takes place by means of\n_____\n,\n_____\nand\n______\n.\nAns\n: Wind, insect, water"
